(b) The duty of implementation and enforcement of these regulations rest with the Pierce County Board of Commissioners, and by virtue of this ordinance is hereby expressly delegated to the Pierce County Board of Health who is hereby charged with promulgation of sufficient procedures for insuring compliance with these rules and regulations by the citizens of Pierce County or those individuals found within the boundaries of Pierce County. The Pierce County Board of Health is directed to implement procedures which will insure that the citizens of Pierce County or those individuals found within the boundaries of Pierce County will receive all procedural rights to which they are entitled under the laws of the State of Georgia.
(c) Any violation of the rules and regulations hereby referenced shall be a violation of this section and shall be a misdemeanor offense. Any violator shall be subject to the imposition of a fine not to exceed $1,000.00 and/or imprisonment for a period not to exceed sixty (60) days. Any failure of payment of inspection fees listed within the fee schedule adopted by Pierce County Board of Health and approved the Pierce County Board of Commissioners within 60 days of first notice, may result in suspension of permit.
(d) The Magistrate's Court of Pierce County shall have jurisdiction over violators of this section and all procedures for enforcement of such section shall be as provided in O.C.G.A. Article 4, Chapter 10 of Title 15. Complaints of violation of any provision of this ordinance shall be brought before the magistrate's court by a designated representative of the Pierce County Board of Health and shall be prosecuted through that court.
